              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            Because it's a relatively inexpensive, fast weekend project with real visual payoff, basement floor paint is also one of the most over-promised categories in the home improvement aisle. Product labels frequently use words like "waterproof" and "moisture-blocking" in ways that are technically accurate for surface splashes and light dampness but wildly optimistic for a slab under real hydrostatic pressure. Treat every "waterproof" claim on a can of floor paint as marketing shorthand for "resists surface moisture better than bare concrete," not as a substitute for an actual waterproofing system.
          </p>
